 long short‐term memory#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#A healthy nutrition suggestion model for indian women sports players & active youth using long short‐term memory#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#A healthy nutrition suggestion model for indian women sports players & active youth using long short‐term memory#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/GHV8N4C6","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/9XQZFTSD?page=1&annotation=ALD6F6YZ","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/9XQZFTSD?page=2&annotation=PY4G46TZ","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 3","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/9XQZFTSD?page=3&annotation=Q77GAJ4Y","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 4","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/9XQZFTSD?page=4&annotation=Y9V6RCP6","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/9XQZFTSD?page=6&annotation=ENVGJV67","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 4","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/9XQZFTSD?page=4&annotation=QB8Z88F4","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/9XQZFTSD?page=6&annotation=JDGJP7HU","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"A healthy nutrition suggestion model for indian women sports players & active youth using long short‐term memory","Authors":"Keerthana Ramaraj, Valliammal Narayan, Thookanayakanpalayam Thyagarajan Dhivyaprabha, Parthasarathy Subashini","Year":2024,"DOI":"10.1002/itl2.452","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"In this paper an intelligent food recommendation system based on Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) and LSTM with GRU is proposed to suggest meals for women athletes.In order to build an intelligent model, many related works are referred and presented in this section. Sports nutrition-based recommendation systems are composed of software, dashboard, and mobile applications which are developed based on machine learning and deep learning algorithms. These works help to build an intelligent recommender system in an effective way.To make a prediction and to suggest the foods to the players, a model should be deployed. The pre-processed data is called and the model is built with LSTM and further extended with LSTM with GRU. The proposed system is deployed with LSTM and LSTM with GRU. In both models, sequential data is declared for defining the model, and the layers are added to it.  Both models use an activation function for cell state and node output but LSTM with GRU uses an update gate to train the model in an efficient and simple way. The algorithms are capable of processing small and long sequences of input resources without increasing the network size, so it performs better way for classification. In our prediction, the input variables are age, height, and weight. The cell is responsible remembers the values over time intervals so memory stores them.The experiments were performed using a Jupytper Notebook Google colab in 2C+3G 2.60GHz processor used for doing the experiments in the model. The training–testing splitting procedure is used to estimate the performance of the algorithm for model building. This procedure is dividing the data into training and testing sets. The training set is used to fit the model for predicting results and the testing set is to evaluate the performance of the model. The data is divided by the k-fold method with a ratio of 70% training and 30% testingIn this paper, an intelligent diet recommendation system is developed that suggests Indian nutritional foods to enhance the performance and endurance recovery of women athletes","Findings":". As a result LSTM with GRU works better with high accuracy and other metrics using the tanh activation function. So further the output nutrition foods of LSTM with GRU are mapped to the interface","Conclusions":"In the future, this system can be advised to athletes to intake recommended foods for a specific period of time and measure their physical outcomes in a real-time environment.","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"l36vdw","at":1774939668837}},"smart_blocks:ramarajHealthyNutritionSuggestion2024.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.01942352,0.0699193,-0.03299,-0.01171088,0.02047601,0.02354678,-0.04962445,0.06295505,0.05099227,-0.03603799,0.01917558,-0.10508896,-0.00561197,0.08141382,0.04542838,-0.0666845,0.03876772,-0.0021669,0.01118421,-0.03085484,0.07411722,-0.05964112,-0.01296847,0.00175503,0.04079915,-0.02217758,0.01382866,-0.05116157,-0.08947282,-0.21829878,0.02806567,-0.03011296,0.07393022,0.01706648,-0.09668714,0.00717596,0.00333369,0.00640817,-0.05177292,0.03609876,0.00302149,0.01407521,0.04606839,0.00488534,0.03459772,-0.00887463,-0.05255676,-0.02060901,-0.04720308,-0.00723956,-0.03521969,0.01935721,0.03427505,0.0043296,0.02006054,0.03577821,0.03853499,0.03989524,0.00334652,0.09787051,0.0394017,0.03272224,-0.1938016,0.02526026,-0.01227542,0.03849004,-0.04541694,0.03094436,-0.00096766,0.02550074,-0.02177392,0.05958521,0.0478166,0.01006531,0.01445097,0.04014966,0.04965201,0.01835525,-0.01600567,0.02008748,-0.01543299,0.02532894,-0.02510422,-0.05248237,-0.02660587,-0.0337951,-0.03629883,-0.07121536,0.02204833,-0.07323382,-0.01384661,0.03961161,0.00464765,0.07861711,0.01903098,-0.02223164,-0.00662299,0.01149481,-0.09980873,0.12556036,-0.08148092,0.02712426,0.00791349,0.00794852,0.00316111,-0.06445659,-0.06062671,-0.00186901,-0.02272258,0.02600794,-0.00790839,0.04376169,-0.00450034,0.03339143,-0.01804736,0.04193311,0.10401424,0.00956934,0.01089703,0.00482395,-0.07058815,0.01221159,0.0251675,-0.01580875,0.01289869,-0.01483941,-0.02068391,0.03460113,0.04440977,0.0438011,0.0262876,-0.0232918,-0.08415417,-0.01751059,0.035668,0.0201031,0.07747209,-0.04370179,0.01598086,0.00514358,-0.027319